        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "451eccd5-af99-536e-bc39-5f4256c837c6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Grand Hyatt New York, Grand Central Terminal, Midtown Manhattan, New York City\n- Products: Commodore Hotel\n- People: Donald Trump, John Steber\n- Events: 1945 NFL Draft\n- Organizations: National Football League\n- Roles: President of the United States\n\nFacts:\n- The Commodore Hotel was originally built and opened on January 28, 1919, and it later became the Grand Hyatt New York.\n- The 1945 National Football League Draft was held on April 8, 1945, at the Commodore Hotel in New York City, New York.\n- John Steber was drafted in the seventh round with the 61st overall pick of the 1945 NFL Draft.\n- Donald Trump was born on June 14, 1946.\n- In 1980, Donald Trump modernized the exterior of the Commodore Hotel building and renovated its interior as part of his first construction project in Manhattan.\n- Donald Trump has served as the 45th and current President of the United States since January 20, 2017.\n- The Grand Hyatt New York is a hotel directly east of Grand Central Terminal in Midtown Manhattan, New York City.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "ad32c873-814a-5636-9aab-de8ca5ebbe6e",
        "text": "Page: Grand Hyatt New York. Sentence: The Grand Hyatt New York is a hotel located directly east of the Grand Central Terminal in Midtown Manhattan, New York City.\nPage: Grand Hyatt New York. Sentence: It was originally built and opened on January 28, 1919, as The Commodore Hotel.\nPage: Grand Hyatt New York. Sentence: In 1980, Donald Trump modernized the outside of the building and renovated the inside as part of his first construction project in Manhattan.\nPage: Donald Trump. Sentence: Donald John Trump (born June 14, 1946) is the 45th and current President of the United States, in office since January 20, 2017.\nPage: 1945 NFL Draft. Sentence: The 1945 National Football League Draft was held on April 8, 1945, at the Commodore Hotel in New York City, New York.\nPage: John Steber. Sentence: He was drafted in the seventh round (61st overall) of the 1945 NFL Draft.",
